LIMITED GRANT FOR VERIFICATION OF THE ACCOMPANYING PAPER
========================================================

A snapshot of this software, frozen at a single recorded revision, is distributed as
part of the research artifact accompanying the paper

    "Call-by-Structure: Preserving Visual Structure During Evaluation of
     Block-Based Programs"

so that the source-level claims made in that paper can be checked against a fixed
tree. With respect to that snapshot, and to no other version of this software,
L-Workshop grants the following.

1. DISTRIBUTION AS PART OF THE ARTIFACT. To the authors of that paper, and to any
   publisher, conference, journal, or archive that hosts or preserves the artifact:
   a non-exclusive, royalty-free, worldwide right to reproduce and distribute the
   snapshot verbatim, as an integral part of that artifact and not as a standalone
   work.

2. RETENTION AND EXAMINATION. To any person who receives that artifact: a
   non-exclusive, non-transferable, royalty-free right to retain a copy of the
   snapshot and to read, build, execute, and test it, for the sole purpose of
   examining, reproducing, or evaluating the claims made in that paper.

   The right in (2) expressly includes the operations the artifact's own
   documentation asks a reader to perform: installing its declared dependencies,
   running its build, and running its test, conformance and table-generation
   harnesses — including the λ_Vis conformance and paper-table harnesses the
   artifact drives through ../run_blc.sh — together with the local build outputs
   and regenerated data files those operations produce. It also extends to whatever
   local, temporary modification is genuinely necessary to carry out such an
   examination — for example instrumenting a file in order to observe its
   behaviour. It does not permit distributing a modified copy.

3. DURATION. The rights in (1) and (2) are perpetual and irrevocable with respect to
   copies of the artifact already distributed, so that the published scientific
   record remains verifiable.

RESERVATION. All other rights are reserved. In particular, nothing above permits:
use of this software, in whole or in part, in any other product, service, publication,
or derivative work; redistribution of the snapshot apart from the artifact;
sublicensing; removal or alteration of copyright or licence notices; or any commercial
use. No rights are granted in any revision of this software other than the snapshot
described above.

